        <p>Farm Fire at Appleton. Two stacks, one of hay and one of corn, were com- pletely destroyed by a fire which broke out about midnight on Thursday at the Beehive Farm, Appleton, in the occupation of Mr. Warburton. Both the War- ; rington and Wilderspool brigades were soon on the spot, the former not being required, however. The Wilderspool men were engaged until two o'clock yesterday afternoon. op. Recent excavations in Rome show that dentistry was practised many centuries ago. On the Via Rosella, which existed at the time of the old Roman Republic, a cave has been opened which disclosed a number 'f graves set in niches. One skeleton was found with a perfectly modelled set of gold teeth.</p>
